  "term": "life history",
  "definition": "In this context, life history refers to a person’s developmental pattern or calibration as shaped by childhood environment. In life-history theory, it is described in terms of trade-offs along a fast-to-slow continuum and used to study how early and current environments relate to later judgments.",
